sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 task, R2-R4 (process.stop shape: 209, @swamp/ssh, full intent as inputs), DECISIONS instance.run_steps (commands as inputs, sudo -u intent account, terminal projection, no API reads). docs/reference/instance-setup.md.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: instance:setup
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as app-dev Node<br/>reached over ssh
  CLI->>GW: instance:setup 42<br/>--idempotency-key=KEY
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit instance:setup 42`
  %%> - syntax: `instance:setup <instance> [--idempotency-key=KEY] [--json]`
  %%> Input:
  %%> - the numeric Instance ID
  %%> Who can call it:
  %%> - the `orbit` CLI and the MCP tool send the same request
  Note over GW: Validate, record the task<br/>Instance 42 · task #5133
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - your Node has an access grant to Node 12, the Node of Instance 42
  %%> - Instance 42 is an active development Instance on an `app-dev` Node
  %%> - no other task holds Instance 42; the Gateway holds one lock per Instance and waits briefly for a busy one
  %%> Records:
  %%> - the Project's setup steps as they are now: names, commands, timeouts, and their digest
  %%> - a later change to the list does not change this task; start a new one to use it
  %%> Result:
  %%> - task #5133 recorded with the full intent
  %%> - nothing has happened on the Node yet
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-instance-setup · 550 s
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - starts one Swamp run on serve (Node 209)
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - `kind`: instance.run_steps
  %%> - every step's name, command and timeout
  %%> - the checkout path, the Instance account and the Node's Vite+ store (`VP_HOME`)
  %%> - the seed: `ORBIT_SEED_PATH` and `ORBIT_SEED_COMMIT` of the `default` Instance on Node 12
  %%> - Node 12's address and SSH host keys; the SSH identity comes from the `swamp` role
  %%> Budget:
  %%> - 550 s for the whole list; the step timeouts add up to at most 540 s
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5133
  %%> What you get:
  %%> - the task number, at once
  %%> Next:
  %%> - the CLI follows the task with `operation:show`
  SW->>N: Check the checkout<br/>@swamp/ssh · owned, on branch
  %%> How:
  %%> - Swamp reaches Node 12 over SSH from 209 with the official `@swamp/ssh` behavior
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - checks that the checkout of Instance 42 exists and is the one Orbit owns
  %%> - checks that the Instance account exists
  %%> Why:
  %%> - the commands run only in the checkout the intent names
  loop each setup step, in order
    SW->>N: Run setup step<br/>sudo -u · timeout · bash -eu
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - runs one step's command with `bash -eu` from the repository root of the checkout
    %%> - with `VP_HOME`, `ORBIT_SEED_PATH` and `ORBIT_SEED_COMMIT` set
    %%> Typical steps:
    %%> - `composer install`
    %%> - `vp install`
    %%> - `php artisan migrate`
    %%> Runs as:
    %%> - the Instance account from the intent, with `sudo -u`; not root
    %%> Limits:
    %%> - `timeout` stops the step's whole process group at its own timeout, so no command keeps running after it
    %%> Progress:
    %%> - each step shows under its own name
    %%> Not kept:
    %%> - command text and stdout; only the exit code and a redacted stderr tail
  end
  alt every step exits 0
    N-->>SW: exit 0 for each step
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - each step's exit code; that is the end state, so no other check runs
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event and reads the run's outputs; Swamp never calls the Gateway
    Note over GW: Record result<br/>setup: done · task succeeded
    %%> Result:
    %%> - Instance 42's setup is recorded as done, and an earlier failed step is cleared
    %%> - task #5133 succeeds; an empty list also succeeds
  else a step fails or times out
    N--xSW: exit ≠ 0 or timeout
    %%> When:
    %%> - a command exits with an error or runs past its timeout
    %%> - exit 127 or 126: the command is missing or not executable
    %%> Effect:
    %%> - later steps do not run
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>failed_step, error_code
    %%> The Gateway reads:
    %%> - the failed step, its exit code and the redacted stderr tail
    Note over GW: Keep Instance, mark failed<br/>task failed · rerun from start
    %%> Result:
    %%> - Instance 42 stays active; its setup is marked failed with the step name
    %%> - task #5133 fails with `instance.setup_step_failed`, or `instance.setup_step_unavailable` for a missing command
    %%> On the Node:
    %%> - what earlier steps did stays; there is no rollback and no teardown
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - fix the cause and run `instance:setup` again; it starts at the first step, so steps should converge
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show #5133
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - asks for the task's status every 2 seconds until it has ended
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the current status, and the result once the task has ended
  end
